{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~","id":105491,"title":"~Sidereal as the Martial Art Exalted~","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-04T04:36:33-07:00","id":105491,"title":"~Sidereal as the Martial Art Exalted~","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://i1196.photobucket.com/albums/aa418/crimsonorigami/35842fdc-e8f0-41ad-975e-2758f84e77cd.jpg?t=1396611522\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>~The great Anys-Syn find out what happen when you lie too much about being Creation's most peerless Martial Artist. All those bribe to the Boobs Goddess sure backfire very spectacularly</i>~ <hr /> <div align=\"left\"><br /> So yeah, Sidereal being the the MA Exalted sound extremely stupid in Second Edition, can you imagine the book claiming DB as the Having Sex Exalted (lowly Terrestrial only worthy of being an Exalted of Specialty). They have no native charm that aid them in learning or teaching MA, or charm that evoke the image of Wuxia character, and the ability to use SMA at cheaper cost only come into play at Essence 5 which mean they basically just the same as everyone in the MA apartment at low Essence .</div> </div> <br /> <br /> Not to mention the Martial Arts world in Exalted is so............theme-parked, it's like the author just watch some movies with the Wuxia tag and go on to write SotM or something. I kinda hope that they at least slip some kind of reference from some of Chinese most famous wuxia writer Jin Yong, but no, instead of Thousand Hands Buddha Palm, Divine Gate Thirteen Swords or Nine Yin White Bone Claw we got...well, Scroll of the Monk.<br /> <br /> And thus, I make a wish upon the Maiden that the Sidereal in Third Edition will be a red string of successes instead of failure after failure like the previous one, and someone need to make an information-dumping machine so I can transfer every movie adaption of Jin Yong novels to the writer's heads (I'm serious about Yong being the most successful wuxia writer!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-04-2014, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T05:02:52-07:00","id":105506,"title":"","content":"They do have a native charm for teaching Martial Arts... but only in late 2nd ed, as an expansion from Throne Shadow.<br /> Before Throne Shadow style though, the Sidereal charms were extremely lacking in the themes of being Martial Arts old masters,,, and, honestly, a lot of them seemed more like random effects than the charms of fate-ninja Secret Masters.<br /> <br /> Throne Shadow does make me think the current Devs would like Sidereals to have more charms that actually fit their themes. I know a lot of Sid players like the strange nature of the charmset (if not the mechanical chops of its second ed version) but it does lack a lot of themes.<br /> <br /> I would definitely say that they need to be more than the Martial Arts Exalted, because that's only combat, not social-fu, stealth, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T06:15:35-07:00","id":105534,"title":"","content":"Sidereals having a strong Martial Arts theme isn't in itself a bad thing. The problem really came in as time went on and new Charm concepts and refinements were introduced and the whole &quot;lawl closed Charmset&quot; thing was stubbornly adhered to, meaning that Sids' only real options were to make a Martial Art that incorporated them or completely rewrite 80% of their mechanics. <br /> <br /> Or, as it was, both. <br /> <br /> So you ended up in a situation were, as a Sidreal, you were thrice stupid if you didn't favor Martial Arts ( and Occult). First, you were stupid because that was one of the only ways to expand your power set ( I've joked about making an MA focused on punching forms to process them faster in the past). Second, you were an idiot because that was your only access to new mechanics. And third, you were a moron if you didn't take Throne Shadow, because that was the grab bag all your new things ended up in. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~#post105491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have no native charm that aid them in learning or teaching MA, or charm that evoke the image of Wuxia character, and the ability to use SMA at cheaper cost only come into play at Essence 5 which mean they basically just the same as everyone in the MA apartment at low Essence .</div> </div> </div> </div> Really, the only advantage they had was the Sifu background...which is pretty shit, honestly. Oh, so you can earmark certain styles you want to learn? I can see the clear advantage over, say, the Abyssal with Liege (complete with other benefits and vague at best downsides, particularly compared to the lovingly detailed twin shit punishment mechanics of audits and Paradox) or the Solar who just screams PAST LIFE MEMORY to justify every random thing they want to learn. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And thus, I make a wish upon the Maiden that the Sidereal in Third Edition will be a red string of successes instead of failure after failure like the previous one... </div> </div> </div> Sids jobbing to everyone else and generally being treated to a shit sundae in a dish of shit with shit flavored ice cream topped with shit fudge, shit caramel, shit pecans and a shit cherry on top is, I feel, a rather separate issue to the Martial Arts thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:07:44-07:00","id":105560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~#post105491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The great Anys-Syn find out what happen when you lie too much about being Creation's most peerless Martial Artist. All those bribe to the Boobs Goddess sure backfire very spectacularly</div> </div> </div> </div>Leave my Sifu alone!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:24:10-07:00","id":105563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105560#post105560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leave my Sifu alone!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna draw Miss Syn's boobs being slapped away by Demetheus which leave 2 gapping holes on her chest, but that seem too mean so I settle with ass-drwarf Syn instead ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:53:29-07:00","id":105574,"title":"","content":"One thing to take into consideration about Sidereal role as MA masters is that while Solar (and possibly most others') Charms are intended as building blocks of a character's legendary prowess, not necessarily individual techniques that recognized in-character, the same might not be true of Sidereal Charms. Their constelation-based closed Charmset with each Ability themed around a Scripture approximates much more closely the structured nature of Martial Arts, and I get the distinct impression that Sidereal Charms are individually known and recognized as specific techniques","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T07:55:14-07:00","id":105575,"title":"","content":"I don't think Sids' problem lay with lacking advantages when it comes to learning/using martial arts, especially not after Throne Shadow was introduced. I think the real problem was, the way things were set up, martial arts weren't a very advantageous thing in the first place. High buy-in cost, lots of redundancies, problems with utilizing multiple Styles due to different armor/weapon restrictions and the inability to use multiple Forms effectively, and the fact that SMA tended to be broken in an unfun way, created the impression that being master martial artists isn't a desirable thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T08:41:52-07:00","id":105590,"title":"","content":"I do love it if Sidereal in Ex3 have the ability to cherry-pick charms from MA Style or them having Enhanced effects when using MA Charms, maybe a little too.......broken though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T09:45:32-07:00","id":105628,"title":"","content":"From what we know about 3e martial arts so far, they should make Sids' life much easier:<br /> -Only two tiers, MA and SMA;<br /> -MA can be taught to mortals in the form of Techniques (so you don't have to gimp yourself by learning a subpar TMA if you want to empower mortals with kung fu);<br /> -Can be made to work with any combat Ability (will hopefully lead to a much more equal distribution of combat styles among Sids);<br /> -SMA won't be locked behind elder Essence;<br /> -Extra exp just for learning MA/Sorcery!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T09:55:38-07:00","id":105635,"title":"","content":"You know what would be cool?<br /> <br /> Sids getting the ability to build Evocations off of forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:02:47-07:00","id":105639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105635#post105635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what would be cool?<br /> <br /> Sids getting the ability to build Evocations off of forms.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be awesome, but given how the Devs said Sidereals are the worst at evocations, I doubt it will be a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:10:34-07:00","id":105641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105628#post105628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what we know about 3e martial arts so far, they should make Sids' life much easier:<br /> -Only two tiers, MA and SMA;<br /> -MA can be taught to mortals in the form of Techniques (so you don't have to gimp yourself by learning a subpar TMA if you want to empower mortals with kung fu);<br /> -Can be made to work with any combat Ability (will hopefully lead to a much more equal distribution of combat styles among Sids);<br /> -SMA won't be locked behind elder Essence;<br /> -Extra exp just for learning MA/Sorcery!</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, those seem to make a Martial Artist's life in general much better, which still leave us with the question on what special feature the Sidereal has that make them the Martial Art Exalted. Charm that straight-up accelerate the training speed of MA Style will just make the people who think all Sid's charm as &quot;Build a house using ducktape and potatoes&quot; explode into a million pieces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:37:36-07:00","id":105647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105563#post105563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna draw Miss Syn's boobs being slapped away by Demetheus which leave 2 gapping holes on her chest, but that seem too mean so I settle with ass-drwarf Syn instead ;D</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not above killing people to avenge her honour.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T10:50:41-07:00","id":105655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105641#post105641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, those seem to make a Martial Artist's life in general much better, which still leave us with the question on what special feature the Sidereal has that make them the Martial Art Exalted. Charm that straight-up accelerate the training speed of MA Style will just make the people who think all Sid's charm as &quot;Build a house using ducktape and potatoes&quot; explode into a million pieces.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to tell you, having ran a few Sidereals' campaigns, for once I'd like to see a non-MA Sid. It's dull as fuck when the main thing differentiating the characters mechanically is what second Style they used (second, because the first was invariably VBoS for Secrets of Future Strife and Blade - this was pre-2.5).<br /> <br /> As such, I'd rather not bring Sids' mastery of MA even more to the foreground than it already is. And it is - they learn CMA as good as Solars and better than everyone else, they learn SMA better than Solars both in terms of costs and effectiveness once they hit the Form, their &quot;hero style&quot; is actually a meta-style focused on teaching MA to others, they invented the damn thing in the first place!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:11:26-07:00","id":105663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105655#post105655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to tell you, having ran a few Sidereals' campaigns, for once I'd like to see a non-MA Sid. It's dull as fuck when the main thing differentiating the characters mechanically is what second Style they used (second, because the first was invariably VBoS for Secrets of Future Strife and Blade - this was pre-2.5).<br /> <br /> As such, I'd rather not bring Sids' mastery of MA even more to the foreground than it already is. And it is - they learn CMA as good as Solars and better than everyone else, they learn SMA better than Solars both in terms of costs and effectiveness once they hit the Form, their &quot;hero style&quot; is actually a meta-style focused on teaching MA to others, they invented the damn thing in the first place!</div> </div> </div> </div>Those capstone charms need to be a little open ended for that. Like many missiles bow technique that allow for expansion within a narrow ability. Something that still lets them spend experience and grow. Unless astrology becomes a good place to spend experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:17:04-07:00","id":105668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105655#post105655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have to tell you, having ran a few Sidereals' campaigns, for once I'd like to see a non-MA Sid.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have such fun combat Charms. Generalized Ammunition Technique is <i>right there,</i> holding a quivor full of asparagus and asking how awesome it would be to kill people with them. <br /> <br /> The problem, like I mentioned, is that Martial Arts is so heavily incentivized for Sidereals that it's hard to justify essentially massively nerfing yourself for &quot;flavor.&quot; Just being the one skill they can semi-freely develop for rockets MA far and away above any other combat skill. <br /> <br /> That's the conundrum, innit? If we want Sids to be the &quot;Martial Arts Exalted&quot; or whatever, they need to have some clear advantage in that field, while at the same time having that advantage not be so powerful as to render every other choice a sucker's choice. <br /> <br /> A place to start, I think, is not being afraid to add things to their other 24 Charm trees, even if you have to pull the &quot;there all along&quot; BS, sutras/constellations/closed Charmset be damned. There's really no reason that Murder Moving Fingers Dance <i>has</i> to be a Throne Shadow Charm, frinstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:26:26-07:00","id":105676,"title":"","content":"The closed Charmset is a good idea and it keeps the Sidereals unique in a way no other exalt could be. However, that is an issue in combat. Because in other areas you don't need fifty million charms to keep up with opponents they just work as bells and whistles but in combat every charm that works to up your defense or give you now avenues of attack can determine the battle.<br /> <br /> I still don't think new charms should be added once it's created though. However, it might be necessary to up the number of current charms to more than in the previous two editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:36:13-07:00","id":105683,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with Sidereal Martial Arts was that there was virtually no incentive to start a fight with a Celestial Style and then power up because of Form charm restrictions and the mote costs.<br /> Once I'd mentally decoupled Astrology charms from RotSE I found they were better than SMA at being top draw secret weapons that you only broke out on special occasions. Yes, some of them were &quot;spend xp to move the plot along&quot; but a couple let you steal the show if it was important enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:40:28-07:00","id":105689,"title":"","content":"I thought that the expert Martial Arts theme was a subsection of their shtick of being the Esoteric Mysticism Exalted. Their own Charms are formed in a manner reminiscent of Martial Arts trees, so they have an easier time with the restricted, fixed trees of MA.<br /> <br /> Now if only they all weren't in one Ability...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:47:30-07:00","id":105698,"title":"","content":"I don't think Sidereals need Martial Arts as a theme, so much as &quot;esoterica&quot;. Martial Arts just happen to be one particularly handy variety of esoteric wisdom. I think much progress could be made by doubling down on the importance of that theme, and making sure it's clear that their mastery of MA is just one facet of that, along with their command of astrology, their role as teachers and viziers, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T11:48:18-07:00","id":105700,"title":"","content":"As much as I love both Sids and MAs...I'd really rather they not be &quot;the MA exalted&quot;. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather see Astrology punched up into shape so that it is their first, best response to most situations, and is what they are most known (and feared/respected) for! <br /> <br /> As it is, when 1st and 2nd Editions established Viziers as &quot;peerless martial artists&quot;, what most people *heard* was &quot;the best fighters&quot;...which clearly isn't the case, so it makes people confused. What was meant was that only Sids could *make, practise and teach* the most powerful MA styles, and only Solaroids can learn them otherwise (and even they can't practise them as efficiently, since they can't use discount sutras). This plays into their roles as teachers. Granted, previous editions could have done a better job with mechanically representing the teacher role; we didn't see anything of the sort until late 2E gave us Crane Style, followed up by Throne Shadow. <br /> <br /> I'm confident 3E will rectify this from the start. <br /> <br /> But, yes, Siddies are meant to be great teachers, not strong fighters, hence the &quot;glass jaw&quot; Ox-Body...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T12:12:19-07:00","id":105733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105655#post105655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to tell you, having ran a few Sidereals' campaigns, for once I'd like to see a non-MA Sid. It's dull as fuck when the main thing differentiating the characters mechanically is what second Style they used (second, because the first was invariably VBoS for Secrets of Future Strife and Blade - this was pre-2.5).<br /> <br /> As such, I'd rather not bring Sids' mastery of MA even more to the foreground than it already is. And it is - they learn CMA as good as Solars and better than everyone else, they learn SMA better than Solars both in terms of costs and effectiveness once they hit the Form, their &quot;hero style&quot; is actually a meta-style focused on teaching MA to others, they invented the damn thing in the first place!</div> </div> </div> </div>While I quite understand where the complaints in this thread come from, I'm with Morangias here.<br /> <br /> Let me address a few points:<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals aren't really better at MA than other Exalted</b><br /> <br /> True, as a mechanical matter, and a good thing too. This isn't really much of a 2e-ism, either: even in 1e, Martial Arts were something that Sidereals emphasized and they were just about as good at them as Solars. Which is to say, better than pretty much everyone else. You cannot reasonably make a splat mechanically superior in combat using MA than Solars, or else you've consigned yourself to everyone else having MA as a distinctly second-fiddle option. It already is in some cases!<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals need something to make them stick out!</b><br /> <br /> That's SMA.<br /> <br /> I know this isn't a good answer in 2e, where there's about a style and a half worth of unborked SMA in the game, but this is where the thematic comes in. It's where you start seeing the answer to 'what makes Sidereals martial arts masters?'<br /> <br /> Y'know that 'simple comparison' section in Scroll of the Monk? Here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mundane martial arts master can split a brick<br /> and jump over a hedge.<br /> A Terrestrial martial arts master can split a boulder<br /> and jump over a house.<br /> A Celestial martial arts master can split a city<br /> wall and jump over a mountain.<br /> A Sidereal martial arts master can split a soul<br /> and jump to Yu-Shan </div> </div> </div>This is both a technically valid comparison (sort of- I don't think CMA actually allows city-splitting unless it is a very small city) and practically quite misleading, because it seems to indicate a ramping-up of power. SMA isn't about ramping up power, it's showing off the martial artist's absurd mastery. It's that turtle in Kung-Fu Panda who could disable the big bad villain by lightly tapping him a few times. It's about feeling a light brush on your stomach and looking down to see your body unraveling into nothingness.<br /> <br /> I've seen some accusations that this is essentially sideways progression- just using Martial Arts for things Martial Arts really has nothing to do with. Well... yes. Look, even unbroken SMA styles are powerful as hell, but you can't represent supernal enlightenment simply by doubling the numbers on CMA charms and calling it a day. There's really nothing for SMA to <i>do</i> other than stuff like that.<br /> <br /> So yes. SMA are fairly potent combat charms which also serve a utility role, and are flashy. They are also the advantage that Sidereals get over everyone else, because the very most you can reasonably do for actual combat is make a Sidereal Martial Artist as good at MA as a Solar- and even then, the Solar MAist has a better mote pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals should be better at teaching martial arts</b><br /> <br /> I'm divided on this issue.<br /> <br /> In general, I think people who want Sidereals to be better 'teachers' have the wrong idea in mind. A Sidereal is a premiere advisor, font of all arcane knowledge and- just by default- knower of a thousand dark secrets of Creation. The archetypes they draw from, though, are the great sages who sit on mountains or secretly make the young Emperor wise, not Ms. Frizzle.* They're the masters which appear when the student is ready, not the masters which ready the student. The fact that you don't learn their many powerful secrets easily is a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure that Martial Arts are exactly the same. On the one hand, you've got the above theme covered with SMA, the hard-to-learn yet legendary-secret-styles which only a mighty hero who is already a master could possibly comprehend.** On the other hand, actual Sidereals are mostly going to want to train Terrestrials or promising mortals, or even Exigents. Throne Shadow provided both a means and an incentive to do this, and I can't say that it ruined anything. I wouldn't be unhappy to see Shadow Fingers and related sifu charms return in 3e.<br /> <br /> <b>Martial Arts kinda suck as a combat option</b><br /> <br /> Yeah ):<br /> <br /> Well, we'll see how 3e addresses this, I suppose!<br /> <br /> <b>Sifu</b><br /> <br /> ...is a bad background and should feel bad. Why on earth couldn't this effect be baked into Allies, or maybe some sort of other Mentor thing? If I have the trust of another Sidereal such that they are prepared to teach me their most powerful secret techniques, why wouldn't they be willing to lend me some cash or help guard my house or whatever?<br /> <br /> The answer, obviously, is that Sifu is supposed to invoke the aforesaid 'wise sages who don't leave their monasteries', but Sidereals are also political and practical creatures, with much more complex alliances than that. The background should never have existed.<br /> <br /> <b>Maybe Sidereals are TOO MA-centric?</b><br /> <br /> Morangias brings up an excellent point; every Sidereal character on earth must focus on the progression of their martial arts styles before all else. This is the greatest tragedy of the entire Sidereals book, because it contains the following trees:<br /> <br /> -Sidereal Thrown, AKA 'Unstoppable storm of deadly shadow-blades'<br /> -Sidereal Melee, AKA 'Blind swordsman'<br /> -Sidereal Archery, AKA 'Yes, I am out of arrows. But I am not out of lingerie.'<br /> <br /> And Exalted Modern, of course, has-<br /> <br /> -Sidereal Firearms, AKA 'He's firing his finger-gun at random into the air and <i>it is killing everyone.</i>'<br /> <br /> And aside from Melee, those might as well just not exist because most of your combat charms have to be Martial Arts. <br /> <br /> I have pretty high hopes that 3e will address this problem, hopefully either by creating synergy between native Sidereal trees and martial arts or by incentivizing the purchase of those trees in some other fashion. If that were to happen, I think it's entirely possible that the Sidereals 3e book would actually bring eternal ultimate joy to the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *NOTE: You can totally play Sidereal Ms. Frizzle <i>and you goddamn should.</i><br /> **Not that he would want to under the current paradigm. 'Oh look I spent double exp to learn a charm which costs me 20m 2wp! Sure am glad I didn't waste that on two Solar Melee charms or something!' I think this is a separate issue which doesn't need to be addressed here, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:25:24-07:00","id":105787,"title":"","content":"I have actually played both of my long-term Sidereals without emphasis on their martial arts, because I love their native Charms so much. (Also, I kind of hate the way Martial Arts became das \u00fcberability back in 1E sometime and usually refuse to build characters around it on principle -- Throne Shadow was such a perfect character fit that I actually did take it for my greensid, though.) I completely agree with Mercury and Morangias: I do think Sidereals are too MA-centric, and could do with a step back towards &quot;esoteric wisdom in general.&quot;<br /> <br /> The problem, in addition to those already stated, is progression in longer-term games (which just so happen to be the games I tend to play, so I have a bias.) Over time, Sidereals have two choices -- either take Martial Arts, or grow sideways to master all the different competencies available to them (and then take Martial Arts when they run out). The former deemphasizes the wonderful Sidereal Charmset and thus is suboptimal. The latter, though, becomes the widely-reviled 1E Lunar Problem, particularly in a Sidereal-centric game: the only thing differentiating two Sidereals in battle is their <s>weapon</s> martial art choice. Also suboptimal.<br /> <br /> The suggestion of greater synergy is a good one, but implemented alone it runs straight into choice two, as above. That problem can be delayed but not solved entirely by writing many more Sidereal Charms, as I've more or less come to expect given the size of the other new Charmsets we know about. For me, it comes down to this: Sidereals need a way to grow vertically, in and out of combat, without being locked to MA or Occult as the only options. Personally, I'm hoping Astrology can bear that weight in 3E, or that John and Holden will wow us with something we've never seen and couldn't have expected. Given 3E as advertised, I'm cautiously hopeful for either option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/39-ysadrel","name":"ysadrel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T13:30:54-07:00","id":105790,"title":"","content":"Well, the question you have to ask yourself is this. Which part of the way these things were handled in 2e we talking about here? The broken, badly-written, mechanically-dysfunctional Sidereal charmset, or the broken, badly-written, mechanically-dysfunctional Martial Arts book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T15:30:30-07:00","id":105870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105698#post105698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Sidereals need Martial Arts as a theme, so much as &quot;esoterica&quot;. Martial Arts just happen to be one particularly handy variety of esoteric wisdom. I think much progress could be made by doubling down on the importance of that theme, and making sure it's clear that their mastery of MA is just one facet of that, along with their command of astrology, their role as teachers and viziers, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I like the most. They're the Exalted of Heaven, not of Martial Arts. Martial Arts isn't unique to the Sidereals, but by their scope of power as the Exalted of Heaven, they harness martial arts in esoteric ways. They should be workers and benders of fate, readers and writers of astrology. It is the Maidens who run the cosmos and Heaven, and as such Sidereal charms should be thematically inspired by the Maidens and the Cosmos. I already rewrite my Sidereal animas as not just bright glows by nebulous starry skies and constellations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T16:02:14-07:00","id":105889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=105790#post105790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the question you have to ask yourself is this. Which part of the way these things were handled in 2e we talking about here? The broken, badly-written, mechanically-dysfunctional Sidereal charmset, or the broken, badly-written, mechanically-dysfunctional Martial Arts book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both were an issue. The problem was more the sidereal book which for the second time made Astrology a shitty thing to invest experience in while simultaneously telling you it was on par with SMA and Sorcery as XP sink options. When it should have been and never ever was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T20:55:57-07:00","id":106011,"title":"","content":"And now, for my Blasphemy of the Day...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mentioned above that I'd rather have Sids known for Astrology rather than MA. But I'll go one better. As people have mentioned, Sids are supposed to be the &quot;mystical, esoteric&quot; Exalted, while the Solars are the greatest straight-forward fighters. If I were rebuilding the game from scratch, I'd switch out the Solar and Sidereal &quot;special powers&quot;, giving Sidereals sole access to Adamant Circle Sorcery, while rebranding SMA as &quot;Solar Martial Arts&quot;!<br /> <br /> Granted, SMA probably wouldn't be as &quot;weirdly esoteric&quot; are they are now, in Solar fists. But now that 3E is getting rid of the difference between TMA and CMA, we could just say that Solars/Abyssals/Infernals practice the latter, as the Solar level...Well, it'd need some rejiggering, but it could work. <br /> <br /> Sidereals, otoh, I feel would work perfectly as peerless masters of Astrology and Sorcery. It fits their themes, and even plays into them being the weakest Celestials in physical combat. It may even explain the Usurpation better...<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T21:20:34-07:00","id":106026,"title":"","content":"Mmh, I see Solar Circle Sorcery as kind of &quot;The biggest hammer.&quot; It's something you don't really want to use, but at the same time when you use it to solve a problem it Solves It. However, it's not subtle, it's not cheap, and it's terrifying. These three things really detract from the idea of the Sidereal Exalted using it, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T21:24:55-07:00","id":106028,"title":"","content":"The way Sorcerous Initiation and Spells are learned doesn't presently put any particular emphasis on esoterica; a typical Sidereal just has to pop into Division 147 and find the right bookshelf to learn any spell he wants. So they are some of the best Sorcerers (despite not having SCS), but because of they're the ones with infrastructure, not anything intrinsic to them. I'm eager to see how the new Sorcery and Magical Workings systems will provide hooks Sids can use to gain a more satisfying advantage in that space.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T22:01:38-07:00","id":106042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106026#post106026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmh, I see Solar Circle Sorcery as kind of &quot;The biggest hammer.&quot; It's something you don't really want to use, but at the same time when you use it to solve a problem it Solves It. However, it's not subtle, it's not cheap, and it's terrifying. These three things really detract from the idea of the Sidereal Exalted using it, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything you just wrote applies equally well to Sidereal Martial Arts. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way Sorcerous Initiation and Spells are learned doesn't presently put any particular emphasis on esoterica; a typical Sidereal just has to pop into Division 147 and find the right bookshelf to learn any spell he wants. So they are some of the best Sorcerers (despite not having SCS), but because of they're the ones with infrastructure, not anything intrinsic to them. I'm eager to see how the new Sorcery and Magical Workings systems will provide hooks Sids can use to gain a more satisfying advantage in that space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Walking into a building and picking a book off the shelf may seem mundane when presented that way (and even to the Sid who does so), but the true esoterica is all in how the writer/ST sells it to the reader/player. Remember, that's not just ANY building, that's one of the most important storehouses of sorcerous lore in Heaven, Itself! There can easily be all sorts of passwords, strange guardians, and the like he must bypass to even lay his eyes on that book...<br /> <br /> Besides which, again, a typical Sidereal just has to pop into the celestial dojo in Yu-Shan and find the right Sifu (whether fellow Seer, MA god, or scroll/memory gem) to learn any MA style he wants, so that arguably also doesn't put any particular emphasis on esoterica...unless one plays up that flavor, which can be done for Sorcery, just as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-04T22:06:34-07:00","id":106043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106028#post106028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division 147</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, the Sidereal Convention which decided to move Department 137 to Wing 147 in the Forbidding Manse was not aware that the original wing was carefully selected by Jupiter herself to calibrate Creation's <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fine-structure_constant\" target=\"_blank\">fine-structure constant</a>. Upon the department's relocation, the reduction in the energy of light resulted in a sudden cooling of Creation's climate. After the first and only blizzard ever experienced in Yane, the department was quickly returned to its original location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2404-chant","name":"Chant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2404_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T08:15:08-07:00","id":106274,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106026#post106026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmh, I see Solar Circle Sorcery as kind of &quot;The biggest hammer.&quot; It's something you don't really want to use, but at the same time when you use it to solve a problem it Solves It. However, it's not subtle, it's not cheap, and it's terrifying. These three things really detract from the idea of the Sidereal Exalted using it, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be interesting to see Sidereals with a unique variant of Sorcery. Also, I'm surprised a sidereal wasn't the one to pry the Mantle from salina's cold hands for the access to solar sorcery. I can't honestly believe they would give it to the scarlet empress.\\<br /> <br /> You know the more I think about it. It'd be interesting if Astrology as a sidereal only subset of sorcery rather than it's own unique system. Which would allow for grander effects that don't overlap with SCS.<br /> <br /> Edit- Didn't feel like creating another post for a continuation of this one. But this would mean that Resplendent destinies would have to be changed. Preferable into a charm. Man, the more I read loom snarling deception the madder I get. Yes, Fiends are solar tier but this is a better version than resplendent destinies at being resplendent destinies which is an entire section in the sidereals section. That's really bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-05-2014, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T11:31:11-07:00","id":106406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106042#post106042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything you just wrote applies equally well to Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not.... really?<br /> <br /> Sidereal Martial Arts are an esoteric enlightenment into how certain things in the universe work, or how many beings have determined emotions or other things should be. They're statements backed up with incredible displays of power sometimes, other times being as subtle as a a single blade of grass in a field.<br /> <br /> Solar Circle Sorcery is Ridiculous Absurd Power. It's the kind of power the Primordials used to communicate with each other through their various states, and reflects their idiosyncrasies in many forms. It's also the last thing you'd describe as subtle. <br /> <br /> In the right hands, SMA is incredibly cheap to use, can be something nobody knows you're using until too late, and, yes, is terrifying. It's also kind of your assumed state after you learn it, whereas SCS is very much not. Nobody ever really wants to use Total Annihilation, but Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style is pretty much the go-to fighting form for all Sidereals after a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T14:30:43-07:00","id":106521,"title":"","content":"The Sidereals, in my view, are majorly the Exalted who are all about using cleverness and smart use of power to overcome sharp limits on the amount of force they can bring to bear.<br /> If you look at the Sidereal's signature literature inspirations (chiefly the Traveller in Black), that's the sort of characters they are. <br /> <br /> So they have powerful Charms that are heavily circumstantial (e.g. most of their Charms and major Astrology Charms), and weak powers that could nonetheless have broad applicability that allow for versatile use (e.g. minor Astrology), and their Charms are written in a way that encourages players to &quot;think like a Sidereal&quot; and get more out of what their Charms can do.<br /> <br /> And they have a capacity at martial arts to overcome their limits at being able to craft new magic. This also plays really well into their themes because martial arts, as styles in movies, is often all about smartly applying styles to counterpick against other styles.<br /> <br /> I think it's useful to note that they don't get martial arts as &quot;the teacher guys&quot; or &quot;the weird guys&quot; or the &quot;we're the wuxia hero guys&quot; (the last of which Solars are probably better placed to fill in). Instead, it's an extension of how the Sidereals get odd powers that nonetheless have useful applications in order that the players get to experience the fun of being a Sidereal, a hero who uses his fundamentally human quality of supreme insight, pragmatism, common sense and efficiency to overcome limits and restrictions to their force and power and manipulate Fate into a human shape (for better or worse).<br /> <br /> (This isn't to say they're &quot;smarter&quot; Exalted, just that they are placed to be smarter on a different, &quot;meta&quot; (ugh a term I usually hate) level, where they're smart, if not wise, about managing and using their powers, rather than their powers expressing genius and smartness, directly through the power.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T02:44:16-07:00","id":106801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106274#post106274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, the more I read loom snarling deception the madder I get. Yes, Fiends are solar tier but this is a better version than resplendent destinies at being resplendent destinies which is an entire section in the sidereals section. That's really bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't feel too bad! It's also way better than Lunar shapeshifting magic at disguises and notably better than Solar and Abyssal disguise magic.<br /> <br /> *quietly weeps*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Once, there was a maiden... who spent all her time on the internet.<br /> &quot;Someone out there is WRONG,&quot; she said.<br /> So she tossed a noose made of golden light... and strangled her opponent.<br /> Both of them died alone.<br /> &quot;Love is for football players and cheerleaders,&quot; her obituary said.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/261-notthepenguins","name":"notthepenguins","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"359"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T03:51:38-07:00","id":106812,"title":"","content":"It's supposed to be restricted by the way you can't disguise yourself as a particular person, which is a big disadvantage... but that's a little undefined.<br /> One player I know would make his character look like someone but with a mole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T05:00:35-07:00","id":106836,"title":"","content":"In addition to being vaguely Loom Snarling Deception has another problem in that (like much of the Infernal charmset) it's written under certain assumptions that clash with how the fanbase has come to view Yu-Shan and Outside Fate.<br /> Was anyone else amazed the first time they saw the Blasphemy keyword? None of my Sidereal PCs prior to that book could really imagine the Aerial Legion mobilizing a rapid response without a political agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T11:40:16-07:00","id":107001,"title":"","content":"Yeah, no kidding. It flew in the face of literally everything else in the setting we've ever been told about Yu-Shan, and the gods' need to make everything into politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T12:45:16-07:00","id":107029,"title":"","content":"Well... Yes and no. I'd say it was an outright acknowledgement (though not the very first) of something that had mostly been vaguely implicit; Heaven can't *just* be a bunch of bureaucratic fuckwits. At the end of the day the work they do is actually important, and if there's one thing the usurper government is going to have standing (if underused) machinery to deal with it's any hint of the usurped government coming back. Various individual gods can be bribed to do jobs that they don't really have much personal stake in (and that mostly just effect earth-bound mortals anyway) poorly or differently or whatever, but the Yozi? That shit is for *real*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T13:11:22-07:00","id":107044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107029#post107029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... Yes and no. I'd say it was an outright acknowledgement (though not the very first) of something that had mostly been vaguely implicit; Heaven can't *just* be a bunch of bureaucratic fuckwits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did say 'the fanbase' for a reason.<br /> Edit: To clarify, a lot of people have done games of Exalted where the PCs saved the world without so much as a nod of approval from Yu-Shan. Then you've got things like the Sidereal response to the Locust Crusade a canonical example of the Sidereal love of red tape being taken to a cartoonish level. Even a lot of Sidereal games tend to be the PCs as the rookies who stumble upon an important case that everyone else is ignoring due to &quot;what's to be done about these Solar Exalted!?&quot; being the common sense destroying agenda of everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-07-2014, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T23:47:22-07:00","id":107276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106406#post106406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sidereal Martial Arts are an esoteric enlightenment into how certain things in the universe work, or how many beings have determined emotions or other things should be. They're statements backed up with incredible displays of power sometimes, other times being as subtle as a a single blade of grass in a field.<br /> <br /> Solar Circle Sorcery is Ridiculous Absurd Power. It's the kind of power the Primordials used to communicate with each other through their various states, and reflects their idiosyncrasies in many forms. It's also the last thing you'd describe as subtle.<br /> <br /> In the right hands, SMA is incredibly cheap to use, can be something nobody knows you're using until too late, and, yes, is terrifying. It's also kind of your assumed state after you learn it, whereas SCS is very much not. Nobody ever really wants to use Total Annihilation, but Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style is pretty much the go-to fighting form for all Sidereals after a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of their nature (which is &quot;just fluff&quot;, and can be changed to suit our needs), the two still have much in common. SMA are very expensive, and though there are ways to cut the costs (would they even be so expensive if Sids were the ONLY ones who could use them?), there are ways to do the same with sorcery (Adamant spells could have the sutras, as an obvious fix).<br /> <br /> As for subtly, I'm sure no one wants to have to use the pinnacle charms of BoKL or CPoC styles, either. <br /> <br /> I will agree that much more of SMA are subtle than sorcery, as they currently stand. But, just as I mentioned repurposing SMA to fit Solar themes and imagery better (whatever that might end up looking like; any ideas?), the same could also be done with Adamant Sorcery so that it *would* fit the Siddies better. I agree, just switching them AS IS would be almost as dumb as giving Abyssals shapeshifting Knacks!<br /> <br /> But with the proper alterations, this could work well. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T00:05:19-07:00","id":107287,"title":"","content":"I can't really imagine SMA as the Solar's top-tier power idea, because SMA were ludicrous in their expanse, not to mention at the same time limited to exploring everything through a degenerate form of punching. They had to be, because the only way the Sidereals could expand their Charmset was through SMA. Now, imagine if they didn't have that, at all, with their limited Charmset, and then you give them SCS. They're utterly fucked, because now it's going to be a situation where they need to spend three turns to use one of their top-tier abilities, during which they are totally helpless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sure, there's no way to canonically do it, but Exalted allows you to knee canon in the crotch and rifle through its pockets to take what you need while it whimpers on the ground. - mockery","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/374-nocte-ex-mortis","name":"Nocte ex Mortis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar374_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T06:59:37-07:00","id":107419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nocte ex Mortis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107287#post107287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really imagine SMA as the Solar's top-tier power idea, because SMA were ludicrous in their expanse, not to mention at the same time limited to exploring everything through a degenerate form of punching. They had to be, because the only way the Sidereals could expand their Charmset was through SMA. Now, imagine if they didn't have that, at all, with their limited Charmset, and then you give them SCS. They're utterly fucked, because now it's going to be a situation where they need to spend three turns to use one of their top-tier abilities, during which they are totally helpless.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean they have to prepare everything to be useful? You mean like turning on three form charms before 2.5 and all the fucking MA aids. Gee parish the thought of having powers that are not only time consuming powers to activate but also 90% of the time can be negated by scene long anti-keyword charms... Oh wait.<br /> <br /> The only difference is that sidereals would have sightly less of a place in personal combat (Which from everything both editions have told us is something they shouldn't be getting into at high essence) and more of an extremely powerful utility tool. Which to be honest. Would be a pretty sweet trade. It won't happen but SMA verses SCS and SCS kind of makes more sense due to the theme of being rather lacking in physical prowess but having mystical might to make up for it.<br /> <br /> Though I would have to say. It'd be interesting if the Sidereals had access to both with the ability to teach it to anyone who could learn it.<br /> <br /> I still think Astrology would be better off using sorcery resplendent destinies and resplendencies retooled into a charm than a completely lame system of checks and minuses that we have now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-07-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T08:48:16-07:00","id":107465,"title":"","content":"I know a lot of people appreciate Sidereals the way they are. IMO, I'm not entirely comfortable with Sidereals being based on the &quot;kung fu hermit&quot; or the &quot;legendary kung fu master&quot;. I think that those archetypes may end up forcing them as NPC's. Sure they also have all the &quot;secret agent&quot; stuff, but in the light of the Ex3 I feel like I can't see Sids as cool as I see solars and lunars now (based on the mythical hero and the mythical beast respectively). If the solar is Hercules, and the lunar could be the nemean lion, who would be the sidereal within this same myth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T08:55:55-07:00","id":107469,"title":"","content":"What Epi said. <br /> <br /> Alas, I realize that this would never happen; even if the devs thought it was a great idea, it'd be TOO much of a departure from previous editions, and they'd likely think the fans would lynch them if they tried to change things that much. Which might actually be the case!<br /> <br /> The best way to move forward with what we have, IMO, is to buff Astrology up to the point where Sidereal allies and enemies respectively want and fear to see them activating Astrological powers instead of MA forms. I suppose this would necessitate downplaying/nerfing SMA, but considering that it never really worked in the first place, and that 3E seems to be doing so anyway, why not?<br /> <br /> To compensate, Astrology should be more immediately useful and effective, meaning that it can be used instantly, in Creation, by a lone Sid and has some significant effect on targets, even if they're outside of Fate. We can keep the time-consuming, involved rituals up in Heaven, but buff them up so that they truly do shape the face of the earth as they are hyped to (factional infighting and the Great Curse keeps this from being abused, unless the PCs are epic enough to bring most of the Fellowship around to one POV)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T08:59:42-07:00","id":107474,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, and I'm not in any way withdrawing my wish that it were possible to make a fun, playable Sid character without diving headfirst into MA, SMA is more appropriate for Sids than Sorcery because to me, Sorcery seems to be about knowing whereas SMA is about understanding.<br /> <br /> Sorcery has things like, you know the secret Sign of Peace that prevents people from fighting in your presence. You know of the horrible Eyeless Face and know how to exploit the cracks in the walls of his prison to call his minions to your service. You know the names of ten thousand demons and the ancient surrender oaths that let you enslave them.<br /> <br /> With SMA, you understand a fundamental truth about the nature of the world and reassert said truth through your martial techniques. You understand the underlying patterns of Creation's essence and thus you can use the techniques of Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Style. You understand that identity is just a glitch in your essence pattern and express said understanding through Kaleidoscopic Borders of Logic*. So on, so forth.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is very thematic for Solars, as it is about imposing your will upon the world. SMA is very thematic for Sids, as it exploits the esoteric system of Creation while still working within it.<br /> <br /> If having access to the highest tier of sorcerous power was to be the Sids' shtick, it would have to look and feel quite different from what we know as Exalted's Sorcery. Likewise, if Solars had their own way of achieving blatantly magical effects through martial training and philosophical understanding, it'd have to look quite unlike SMA to remain in theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:09:32-07:00","id":107480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107474#post107474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If having access to the highest tier of sorcerous power was to be the Sids' shtick, it would have to look and feel quite different from what we know as Exalted's Sorcery. Likewise, if Solars had their own way of achieving blatantly magical effects through martial training and philosophical understanding, it'd have to look quite unlike SMA to remain in theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting points!<br /> <br /> But, just as a thought exercise, let's say that we WERE going ahead full-steam with this approach. What should high level MA and Sorcery look like in Solar and Sidereal hands, hypothetically-speaking?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T09:38:34-07:00","id":107497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107465#post107465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot of people appreciate Sidereals the way they are. IMO, I'm not entirely comfortable with Sidereals being based on the &quot;kung fu hermit&quot; or the &quot;legendary kung fu master&quot;. I think that those archetypes may end up forcing them as NPC's. Sure they also have all the &quot;secret agent&quot; stuff, but in the light of the Ex3 I feel like I can't see Sids as cool as I see solars and lunars now (based on the mythical hero and the mythical beast respectively). If the solar is Hercules, and the lunar could be the nemean lion, who would be the sidereal within this same myth?</div> </div> </div> </div>In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/78589-kickstarter-update-57-at-long-last?p=79037#post79037\">the post</a> where he likened Solars to myth-heroes and Lunars to monsters and beasts, John likened Sidereals to agents of myth. They're facilitators of what goes on: the story might not have taken the shape and trajectory it did without them being in the right place at the right time, or it might have been less likely to work out &quot;the right way&quot; without their interference. They are actors whose presence may never even go noticed -- or noticed as other than the characters they play, at any rate.<br /> <br /> For the tale of the Nemean Lion, perhaps the Sidereal assumes the role of King Eurystheus or more likely one of the king's advisors, to set the task before Hercules to begin with, or of someone Hercules meets along the way to give him extra incentive (one version speaks of a boy who will sacrifice a lion to Zeus if Hercules kills the beast in 30 days, or else the boy will sacrifice himself), or someone who drops the hint that perhaps Hercules's knife would fail to skin the beast's nigh impenetrable hide, but the beast's own claws might do the trick (Athena does this in at least one version). Or, if the Sidereal's committed, maybe playing (or arranging for) all three encounters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 04-07-2014, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T12:33:06-07:00","id":107613,"title":"","content":"Thanks, that was very illustrative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T13:18:41-07:00","id":107640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107497#post107497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/78589-kickstarter-update-57-at-long-last?p=79037#post79037\">the post</a> where he likened Solars to myth-heroes and Lunars to monsters and beasts, John likened Sidereals to agents of myth. They're facilitators of what goes on: the story might not have taken the shape and trajectory it did without them being in the right place at the right time, or it might have been less likely to work out &quot;the right way&quot; without their interference. They are actors whose presence may never even go noticed -- or noticed as other than the characters they play, at any rate.<br /> <br /> For the tale of the Nemean Lion, perhaps the Sidereal assumes the role of King Eurystheus or more likely one of the king's advisors, to set the task before Hercules to begin with, or of someone Hercules meets along the way to give him extra incentive (one version speaks of a boy who will sacrifice a lion to Zeus if Hercules kills the beast in 30 days, or else the boy will sacrifice himself), or someone who drops the hint that perhaps Hercules's knife would fail to skin the beast's nigh impenetrable hide, but the beast's own claws might do the trick (Athena does this in at least one version). Or, if the Sidereal's committed, maybe playing (or arranging for) all three encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny, when I read that post by John, I thought more of such occurrences like the Angel coming down to wrestle Jacob or Buddha subduing the Monkey King. Guys speaking for the very authority the myth hero wants to subvert and the monster wants to destroy, stepping down and trying to get the story back on tracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T13:19:01-07:00","id":107642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107497#post107497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/78589-kickstarter-update-57-at-long-last?p=79037#post79037\">the post</a> where he likened Solars to myth-heroes and Lunars to monsters and beasts, John likened Sidereals to agents of myth. They're facilitators of what goes on: the story might not have taken the shape and trajectory it did without them being in the right place at the right time, or it might have been less likely to work out &quot;the right way&quot; without their interference. They are actors whose presence may never even go noticed -- or noticed as other than the characters they play, at any rate.<br /> <br /> For the tale of the Nemean Lion, perhaps the Sidereal assumes the role of King Eurystheus or more likely one of the king's advisors, to set the task before Hercules to begin with, or of someone Hercules meets along the way to give him extra incentive (one version speaks of a boy who will sacrifice a lion to Zeus if Hercules kills the beast in 30 days, or else the boy will sacrifice himself), or someone who drops the hint that perhaps Hercules's knife would fail to skin the beast's nigh impenetrable hide, but the beast's own claws might do the trick (Athena does this in at least one version). Or, if the Sidereal's committed, maybe playing (or arranging for) all three encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really good. <br /> <br /> ... but I got the impression the thrust of John's comment was that the Sidereals are literal kung fu agents of mythic forces. Not necessarily engineers and facilitators of myths (although they can be and often are that as well, given the restrictions they work under).<br /> <br /> (Although that's my impression - mystic Kung Fu Master Morke's koans are always neatly expressed, but often open for interpretation in highly individual ways... )<br /> <br /> It's in the context of Solars being defined as heroes who overcome supernatural mythic forces through pure skill and will (&quot;<i>Solars fight, destroy, and ultimately recreate the status-quo, doing so by conquering the obliquely magical through acts of sheer will, force, and skill writ-large, like every myth-hero in literature.</i>&quot;). <br /> <br /> And in this context, Sidereals by contrast are more the literal agents of the gods, who use overtly supernatural powers given by the gods in the service of the gods. That's how they're &quot;agents of myth&quot;.<br /> <br /> (Although they're also agents of myth and the gods for a particular sort of myth and goddess. <br /> <br /> That myth and goddess is at least somewhat the sort of Prometheus or of the Traveller in Black, the sort that reshapes the world into a place where talented humans can prosper and which tames chaotic supernatural forces (even sympathetic ones) and lifts up the rational and sensible (and all that &quot;good&quot; Technocratic kinda jazz) to that end.<br /> <br /> It's also the Fates of the Gods of Pegana, that from time to time pronounce against the gods in place of their mortal playthings, or the inevitability of the way of the world.)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how this would fit in a Hercules story though, unlike your suggestion which is *actually* useful for how Sidereals could fit into that story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T15:55:56-07:00","id":107749,"title":"","content":"Sidereals are kung fu angels and will go biblical on your sorry ass unless you do what you're fucking supposed to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T19:33:10-07:00","id":107898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107497#post107497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/78589-kickstarter-update-57-at-long-last?p=79037#post79037\">the post</a> where he likened Solars to myth-heroes and Lunars to monsters and beasts, John likened Sidereals to agents of myth. They're facilitators of what goes on: the story might not have taken the shape and trajectory it did without them being in the right place at the right time, or it might have been less likely to work out &quot;the right way&quot; without their interference. They are actors whose presence may never even go noticed -- or noticed as other than the characters they play, at any rate.<br /> <br /> For the tale of the Nemean Lion, perhaps the Sidereal assumes the role of King Eurystheus or more likely one of the king's advisors, to set the task before Hercules to begin with, or of someone Hercules meets along the way to give him extra incentive (one version speaks of a boy who will sacrifice a lion to Zeus if Hercules kills the beast in 30 days, or else the boy will sacrifice himself), or someone who drops the hint that perhaps Hercules's knife would fail to skin the beast's nigh impenetrable hide, but the beast's own claws might do the trick (Athena does this in at least one version). Or, if the Sidereal's committed, maybe playing (or arranging for) all three encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal as &quot;Mysterious Ninja that nobody notice&quot; got the same problem as Lunar &quot;Myth Monster&quot;, they are obviously NPC characters that exist to make other character more interesting. Sidereal already got stucked with &quot;Die When Fight&quot; syndrome, no need for &quot;Don't Interact with your Circle 'cause you're Mysterioussss~&quot; and &quot;Every Sidereal has Manipulation 5 with ten thousand sideway plots in Mind&quot;, since they're an actual playable splat, I expect to actually play one without all the baggage you mention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T20:37:57-07:00","id":107939,"title":"","content":"Okay! I'm a full supporter of SMA, but envisioning a 'Sidereal Sorcery' isn't too hard at all. In fact, you can throw one together in about five minutes by taking the entire Astrology system, translating the Resplendencies into minor sorceries, creating a spell to replace the basic Destiny system and making the rest of the spells more-or-less Greater Astrology charms. High power is balanced out by Paradox costs, slap a coat of paint on it.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to take more time to create a more intriguing system, you should look into removing the idea of 'Sidereal Sorcery' as a separate system and instead adapt Astrology so that college dots = dots in the related ability and give a player who invests in a Sidereal tree the ability to create greater astrology 'spells' of that ability's college. This is a notional drop in strength for the Sidereals, but a practical increase in power- since each Ability dot gets you more sorcerous options.<br /> <br /> I know this relies a lot on the Greater Astrology stuff- but that really <i>is</i> exactly the sort of stuff one'd expect to see out of 'Sidereal Sorcery'. I think adapting it toward a new end beats creating a redundant system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107465#post107465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot of people appreciate Sidereals the way they are. IMO, I'm not entirely comfortable with Sidereals being based on the &quot;kung fu hermit&quot; or the &quot;legendary kung fu master&quot;. I think that those archetypes may end up forcing them as NPC's. Sure they also have all the &quot;secret agent&quot; stuff, but in the light of the Ex3 I feel like I can't see Sids as cool as I see solars and lunars now (based on the mythical hero and the mythical beast respectively). If the solar is Hercules, and the lunar could be the nemean lion, who would be the sidereal within this same myth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaius had a good post addressing that point, but if I might expand upon it:<br /> <br /> Focusing too much on pithy descriptions is dangerous, even if it's a great way to communicate a high concept. Sidereals have a very natural entry into the 'legendary kung fu master' archetype, but that's in the same way that a Solar has a natural entry into the 'Master craftsman of Creation' archetype. It's not actually a defining characterization! Instead, let's look at what Hatewheel likes to describe them as, since he's been working on this whole 'quickly and effectively describe the Exalted' pitch:<br /> <br /> '<i>Sorcerer-Bureaucrat agents of Heaven'</i><br /> <br /> This is it, really. Solars are the god-kings of old, returned from banishment to bring glory to a fallen world. Lunars are heroes with monsters within or monsters with heroes within. Sidereals are sorcerer-bureaucrat agents of Heaven.<br /> <br /> This is why I like that turn of phrase so much:<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerer</b> - In this case only nominally refers to Sorcery. Even in 1e, the author of the Sidereal charms considered the high-end charms essentially self-contained sorceries rather than the expansions on ability which were most common. An unusually large percentage of the Sidereal trees are hugely externalized effects- moving cities, vanishing from timelines, cursing someone to unlovability, firing an arrow which becomes grain, sacrificing an army to bind a god. SMA fits here too; while it might technically be an expansion on martial skill, it manifests in things like the ability to slap the illness out of someone or re-align your essence to create a hearthstone. You cannot make a Sidereal who has no strange and powerful sorceries, even if you never buy a dot of Occult.*<br /> <br /> <b>Bureaucrat</b> - This one's more obvious, but no less important. Sidereals are part of a greater bureaucracy, and are connected to ten thousand potential friends and foes through it. It's a source of vast power- access to the illimitable powers of Heaven- and a restraint, since you can never stop being part of that bureaucracy. A Sidereal can move a mountain with a single Charm, but he can't do it without explaining himself to someone down the line.<br /> <br /> <b>Agent</b> - Here's a secret: 'Agent' in the Men In Black sense is not a secondary archetype which applies to some Sidereals and not others. It's a description of how you play Sidereals, a characterization which you can only avoid by willfully subverting it. There's always been a lot of arguing about how one 'fixes Fate glitches'- well, here you have it. You go to the source, investigate what's causing the problem and you neutralize it, usually with extreme prejudice. You have some discretion, of course- that's part of the driving story behind any 'elite secret agent' story- will you follow your orders even if you must betray your principles?<br /> <br /> <b>Of</b> - Oh-ho, I bet you thought I wasn't going to include 'of' in my word-by-word analysis! Well you are totally right.<br /> <br /> <b>Heaven</b> - This is the last piece in the puzzle. What does a Sidereal serve? The Exalted of the Maidens change the story of Creation around to match Destiny's plan, but they also hold a red pen which they could use to make edits to their orders. Is it right to bring two realms to war to prevent catastrophic loss elsewhere in the system? Is it right to watch the scions of the Great Houses tear a teenaged Solar apart? Do 'right' and 'wrong' even matter when the stakes are so high? Is a Sidereal loyal to their own morals? To the system? To a god? To a nation? The Sidereals are the Exalted of Heaven- but have a look at oriental emperors in the real world and see how fickle Heaven can be.<br /> <br /> When you're inside, looking out, playing a Sidereal feels a little like being a mechanic. You've come down into Creation because <i>something</i> has gone tits-up, or is otherwise going to, and you're the only man for the job. You've got a toolbox with a portable hole, an infinitely-extensible piece of chalk, an indestructible length of hose and a fighter jet (it's collapsible), and you will damn well find and fix that problem with this extremely-powerful-if-somewhat-confusing arsenal. Sometimes you come across other people with powerful tools and no direction poking about, and you have to decide if you're going to recruit them, point them to somewhere less risky or break out the fighter jet.<br /> <br /> When you're outside, a Sidereal is like a bizarre combination of Gandalf and Agent K. He shows up, declares that the ring which has been in your family for generations needs to be in a volcano on the other side of the world ASAP, and suddenly the adventure begins. Gandalf K is at once incredibly powerful** and bizarre in his priorities. He's clearly a powerful sorcerer, yet he insists on avoiding all notice and wipes the memory of anyone who notices that something's up.<br /> <br /> ...mind you, this is all for PC Sidereals. Most people who meet a Sidereal do indeed encounter them disguised as someone's evil vizier. That's just a product of limited perception, not a completely different archetypal role.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I think that's cool. Actually, I think it's so cool that I have a hard time playing anything else. Some people feel the other way, and I am happy to let those people play monster-heroes and glorious returned kings while we are sailing through hyperspace on my rowboat and the Exigent is asking me why the fuck we didn't just take the hyperspace-rowboat to Mordor.***<br /> <br /> <br /> *Well, I guess you could just not buy charms? Or maybe only purchase TMA? I digress.<br /> **You can't help but wonder why he doesn't just use that fighter jet to fly the Ring to Mordor. You've got a sneaking suspicion that he hasn't quite told you everything.<br /> ***Because there would have been insufficient time for character development, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T21:28:10-07:00","id":107966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106274#post106274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be interesting to see Sidereals with a unique variant of Sorcery. Also, I'm surprised a sidereal wasn't the one to pry the Mantle from salina's cold hands for the access to solar sorcery. I can't honestly believe they would give it to the scarlet empress.\\<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see that happening, either. But I think Under the Rose implied that Her Redness actually found it in the Imperial Manse, presumably where Salina or whoever last had it, left it...I don't recall, did RotSE note that she currently has it?<br /> <br /> Just wanted to also note that, even if Sids were pulling something like SCS, they wouldn't be totally helpless while activating it. You can still use Dodge Charms as you Shape Sorcery, right? Besides, as Seers have always been made out to be the best at getting things done through others, that fits in well with the canon image of the Solar Sorcerer being protected by her Lunar mate while casting...except the Vizier would be protected by her God-Familiars/Exalted students/Shadow Fingers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 04-08-2014, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T07:17:24-07:00","id":108183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107898#post107898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sidereal as &quot;Mysterious Ninja that nobody notice&quot; got the same problem as Lunar &quot;Myth Monster&quot;, they are obviously NPC characters that exist to make other character more interesting. Sidereal already got stucked with &quot;Die When Fight&quot; syndrome, no need for &quot;Don't Interact with your Circle 'cause you're Mysterioussss~&quot; and &quot;Every Sidereal has Manipulation 5 with ten thousand sideway plots in Mind&quot;, since they're an actual playable splat, I expect to actually play one without all the baggage you mention.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, part of the fun of Exalted is that Perseus and Medusa might team up against Poseidon prompting the Oracle of Delphi to decide what they're doing is too important to leave to chance prompting her to go with them. Also Solar Circles as a team of up to five mythic heroes (as oppose to the hero and their sidekicks) present a similar subversion.<br /> <br /> I'm wary to quote from the &quot;RPGnet version&quot; of Exalted due to stuff like tyrannosauruses in F-16s but this one always makes me smile and it demonstrates my point here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like Moses spent 50 years in the desert learning Jehovah Fist Kung-Fu and then teamed up with Conan, Hercules and Kenshin to fight the Pharoah's jackal-headed ninja armies. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-08-2014, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T08:41:05-07:00","id":108222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107474#post107474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If having access to the highest tier of sorcerous power was to be the Sids' shtick, it would have to look and feel quite different from what we know as Exalted's Sorcery. Likewise, if Solars had their own way of achieving blatantly magical effects through martial training and philosophical understanding, it'd have to look quite unlike SMA to remain in theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree. Sorcery isn't just about imposing your will. It's about preparing and setting up rituals and behaviors and at the end of the day asking a phenomenon to happen. It is grand and flashy but that's pretty much what SMA is. Both are flashy sticks they just have different vectors. Solars pretty much already have the best martial art in the game so it really wouldn't change anything but &quot;Best martial artists&quot; actually being a factual statement instead of pointless hyperbole.<br /> <br /> That being said if Sorcery, Astrology and Martial Arts are supposed to be the three pillars of Sidereal Focus past their charmsets, it would be nice if these three were all Equal rather than MA being the clear and valid choice because Sorcery and Astrology can't ever match up to it. At the very least, if you can't offer such parity then stop pretending these are valid avenues when one hits a wall and the other was never valid in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T09:56:59-07:00","id":108292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108222#post108222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said if Sorcery, Astrology and Martial Arts are supposed to be the three pillars of Sidereal Focus past their charmsets, it would be nice if these three were all Equal rather than MA being the clear and valid choice because Sorcery and Astrology can't ever match up to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help but notice we're still talking about 2e here. I don't think any of these assumptions have any reason to be valid in 3e. This includes the one where Sids have to go outside their native Charmset to remain relevant and have viable answers to problems they face.<br /> <br /> I'm not really interested in discussing how to fix 2e - if it was fixable, I'd still be playing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T10:01:26-07:00","id":108294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108292#post108292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but notice we're still talking about 2e here. I don't think any of these assumptions have any reason to be valid in 3e. This includes the one where Sids have to go outside their native Charmset to remain relevant and have viable answers to problems they face.<br /> <br /> I'm not really interested in discussing how to fix 2e - if it was fixable, I'd still be playing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm referring to 3e. The last two editions this has been the case. If this remains the case then it'll be an issue. Though we know for a fact that they are keeping the closed charmset so it'll be interesting to see what happens to it that would make it so that you don't need something outside of the native charmset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-08-2014, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:03:15-07:00","id":108351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108294#post108294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm referring to 3e. The last two editions this has been the case. If this remains the case then it'll be an issue. Though we know for a fact that they are keeping the closed charmset so it'll be interesting to see what happens to it that would make it so that you don't need something outside of the native charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's important to note that if we gave 2e Sids access to SCS, either alongside or instead of SMA, it wouldn't change anything for them - Solar or Celestial, Sorcery is cumbersome to deal with and not that useful in the long run.<br /> <br /> Basically, there are two layers to the problem Sids have in 2e. The first layer is having a closed, limited native Charmset in a game where only Charms matter. The second layer is none of the options they have for circumventing the first problem being well written or especially useful. Sorcery is only good for cherry picking a few spells, Martial Arts were for the most part broken to the degree of being unplayable, and Astrology was too much buck for too little bang. All three were notorious exp sinks on top of their other problems - but you already know all of that.<br /> <br /> What matters is, with the exception of Astrology, these are universal problems with universal subsystems, and we only associate those problems with Sids because they're saddled with this first problem of their native Charms having too many holes in a system that doesn't forgive having holes in your set of magic tricks.<br /> <br /> Each of those problems requires it's share of attention, but for Sids in particular, it's imperative to make them such that their native Charmset doesn't leave them wide open in situations they are supposed to handle. From what we know so far, the solution proposed by 3e seems to be shifting the focus of the system away from Charm interactions and letting things work without Charms. If this works satisfactorily, then the Sids will be fully playable, pretty much regardless of the shape of Sorcery and MA (which, hopefully, will get satisfactory solutions for their own problems).<br /> <br /> If all these problems are solved, there is no need to change the basic setup of Sids.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T11:34:03-07:00","id":108388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108292#post108292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I can't help but notice we're still talking about 2e here. I don't think any of these assumptions have any reason to be valid in 3e. This includes the one where Sids have to go outside their native Charmset to remain relevant and have viable answers to problems they face.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, 1e and 2e are the two data sets we have information on (or three, if you want to count 2.5). So unless you have an advance copy of Sids 3e to share with the rest of the class (and, should you, I will gladly provide my email address before reporting you to my local Witchfinder General <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) that's kinda what we're stuck talking about. <br /> <br /> And maybe I'm just more pessimistic than you are, but Sidereals being saddled with some massively shite mechanics for two editions running does make me wary of their 3e iteration. I mean, yes, Drive and Firearms on the one hand. But Simple Astrology on the other, which just about the only good to come of it is that it gave me something other than d02 to focus my hat on. <br /> <br /> And really, I've played MMOs for too long to take &quot;It'll be fixed in the expansion, HONEST!&quot; at face value any more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:20:30-07:00","id":108423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108388#post108388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, 1e and 2e are the two data sets we have information on (or three, if you want to count 2.5). So unless you have an advance copy of Sids 3e to share with the rest of the class (and, should you, I will gladly provide my email address before reporting you to my local Witchfinder General <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) that's kinda what we're stuck talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not objecting to that, but I take exception with the way this info gets interpreted in the context of this thread.<br /> <br /> Properly identifying problems is crucial to solving them, and I'm pretty sure people keep getting the different problems with Sids mixed up, thus offering unnecessary, misaimed solutions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:30:16-07:00","id":108443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108423#post108423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not objecting to that, but I take exception with the way this info gets interpreted in the context of this thread.<br /> <br /> Properly identifying problems is crucial to solving them, and I'm pretty sure people keep getting the different problems with Sids mixed up, thus offering unnecessary, misaimed solutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm looking at what the fluff of sidereals is and wanting a solid fluff mechanical coherence. Their limited charmset was supposed to mean they had a complete everything. IT worked in e1. Was awful in e2 it'll be fixed in e3 hopefully. However, what happens after you spend your xp on everything you want? Well the both editions have gone on to say astrology, sorcery and MA. Hopefully, in e3 we won't jerk us around like that this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:41:03-07:00","id":108458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=106011#post106011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned above that I'd rather have Sids known for Astrology rather than MA. But I'll go one better. As people have mentioned, Sids are supposed to be the &quot;mystical, esoteric&quot; Exalted, while the Solars are the greatest straight-forward fighters. If I were rebuilding the game from scratch, I'd switch out the Solar and Sidereal &quot;special powers&quot;, giving Sidereals sole access to Adamant Circle Sorcery, while rebranding SMA as &quot;Solar Martial Arts&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that there are in fact Solars other than Dawns. Twilights need preeminence in the general field of &quot;Sorcery&quot; in the same way that Dawns need it in the general field of &quot;combat.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sidereal Martial Arts don't interfere much with what makes Dawns what they are because they touch on a more thematically specific subset of combat and include a general enlightenment that covers different ground from (say) Solar combat abilities, so you can make Sidereals really good at SMA and do it in a separate way while ensuring the Dawn is still the Dawn. But if you swapped SCS and SMA, you're giving the Dawn an extra powerset he doesn't really need, while taking away something essential to making Twilights what they are.<br /> <br /> Also the different splats cover a lot of ground. especially Solars. There are mystical, esoteric Solars -- that's part of the ground Twilights are meant to cover. Sidereals cover a <i>specific type</i> of mystical esotericism, based on sutras and prayer strips and martial arts enlightenment; they're not meant to be the only type of Exalt that gets any form of contemplative mystical enlightenment ever.<br /> <br /> (Of course, SCS has had issues in the past, even if not quite as bad as 2e SMA. But that's the basic idea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-08-2014, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:55:27-07:00","id":108483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108292#post108292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but notice we're still talking about 2e here. I don't think any of these assumptions have any reason to be valid in 3e. This includes the one where Sids have to go outside their native Charmset to remain relevant and have viable answers to problems they face.<br /> <br /> I'm not really interested in discussing how to fix 2e - if it was fixable, I'd still be playing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although we don't know how 3e Sidereals will work, I believe the devs have implied that MA is still going to be core to being a Sidereal and will generally be vital to your long-term growth. It's a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> Complaints about this coming from 2e are -- well, look, both MA and Sidereals were horrifically broken in 2e (especially SMA, which is supposed the be the pinnacle of how Sidereals approach martial arts!) I don't think that that's a reason to change the underlying Sidereal concept.<br /> <br /> (I would expect that 3e Sidereals are going to look a <i>lot</i> like 1e Sidereals, if updated for 3e's overarching paradigm and mechanics and given more workable Astrology.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T12:59:06-07:00","id":108488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108483#post108483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although we don't know how 3e Sidereals will work, I believe the devs have implied that MA is still going to be core to being a Sidereal and will generally be vital to your long-term growth. It's a feature, not a bug.<br /> <br /> Complaints about this coming from 2e are -- well, look, both MA and Sidereals were horrifically broken in 2e (especially SMA, which is supposed the be the pinnacle of how Sidereals approach martial arts!) I don't think that that's a reason to change the underlying Sidereal concept.<br /> <br /> (I would expect that 3e Sidereals are going to look a <i>lot</i> like 1e Sidereals, if updated for 3e's overarching paradigm and mechanics and given more workable Astrology.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I can't make a character who has 0XP in MA and 1k in Astrology and not have it be workable. Sidereals will have failed me for a 3rd time. I like martial arts. It's cool but having you NEED MA is dumb. No matter how awesome it is that means all sidereals have to become this one stale concept in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T13:23:21-07:00","id":108506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108488#post108488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I can't make a character who has 0XP in MA and 1k in Astrology and not have it be workable. Sidereals will have failed me for a 3rd time. I like martial arts. It's cool but having you NEED MA is dumb. No matter how awesome it is that means all sidereals have to become this one stale concept in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hereby predict that Sidereals will fail you for a third time.<br /> <br /> No, but look- you can make a Sidereal character with 0XP in MA right now! I've done it! I made a Joybringer who was a dabbler Sorcery and a master astrologer*. He was shit at combat and Avoidance Kata'd away whenever things looked too nasty, but that did not upset me because <i>I spent all my xp on Sorcery and Astrology.</i> I made a master sailor in one game, but his total incompetence at leading armies never bothered me. My master assassin was sort of shit at artifact creation, yet did I rage against the unfeeling heavens?<br /> <br /> Now, maybe your complaint is that, Greater Astrology aside, the mechanics of ordinary Astrology will never justify putting 1000xp in? Well, okay. You will also probably not enjoy your mixed Celestials game if you buy every TMA in the game, but buying a few charms to supplement the rest of your character actually works pretty well! Look, I <i>could</i> be wrong, but Astrology has never been a substitute for other magic and I just don't think 3e will expand it into that. I hope that it will be more valuable and incentivize larger investment than current, but putting a thousand xp into Astrology is sort of the thing a very one-trick NPC would do.<br /> <br /> The core of a Sidereal's magic is Sidereal Charms. What does Astrology <i>need</i> to provide to make it 'workable'?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Note: this is after Greater Astrology's introduction because I am not <i>completely</i> bonkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T13:30:15-07:00","id":108510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108506#post108506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, maybe your complaint is that, Greater Astrology aside, the mechanics of ordinary Astrology will never justify putting 1000xp in? Well, okay. You will also probably not enjoy your mixed Celestials game if you buy every TMA in the game, but buying a few charms to supplement the rest of your character actually works pretty well! Look, I <i>could</i> be wrong, but Astrology has never been a substitute for other magic and I just don't think 3e will expand it into that. I hope that it will be more valuable and incentivize larger investment than current, but putting a thousand xp into Astrology is sort of the thing a very one-trick NPC would do.<br /> <br /> The core of a Sidereal's magic is Sidereal Charms. What does Astrology <i>need</i> to provide to make it 'workable'?</div> </div> </div> </div>For as much word count astrology gets and it gets A LOT. Yes it should be a substitute for magic. If it's supposed to be a major pillar of sidereal time and effort. Then yes it shouldn't be this paradox beat stick that greater astrology was. It should be a proper system. One that has it's own set of powers and abilities and has actual uses. It shouldn't be cast aside for the third time because the writers didn't have the time or want to put the effort into making it more than it's been for the last two editions. Which has been a subpar disguise with some neat tricks and a system to break the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 04-08-2014, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:49:22-07:00","id":108686,"title":"","content":"I think Mercury's point is, it'd be more reasonable to expect cheaper, easier to use astrology, than to expect it evolved into something that'd make it worthwhile to invest a thousand experience points in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T15:52:52-07:00","id":108695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108686#post108686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mercury's point is, it'd be more reasonable to expect cheaper, easier to use astrology, than to expect it evolved into something that'd make it worthwhile to invest a thousand experience points in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really isn't reasonable to expect nothing out something that is core to sidereals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T16:11:03-07:00","id":108725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108695#post108695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really isn't reasonable to expect nothing out something that is core to sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology is Sids' unique shtick in the same sense that Knacks are Lunars' unique shtick - it's just putting a system on something they all can do. Still, if somebody expected a worthwhile return on investing a thousand experience points in Knacks, I'd say he's being unreasonable.<br /> <br /> I have this distinct impression you want Astrology to be like Magick from Mage: the Ascension. I don't see it happening any time soon. Doesn't mean I have no expectations whatsoever, just that they're adjusted for scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T18:09:06-07:00","id":108826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108725#post108725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astrology is Sids' unique shtick in the same sense that Knacks are Lunars' unique shtick - it's just putting a system on something they all can do. Still, if somebody expected a worthwhile return on investing a thousand experience points in Knacks, I'd say he's being unreasonable.<br /> <br /> I have this distinct impression you want Astrology to be like Magick from Mage: the Ascension. I don't see it happening any time soon. Doesn't mean I have no expectations whatsoever, just that they're adjusted for scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still spend a thousand and get something rather useful in second edition if you get the high essence knacks. You could spend 1k in astrology and yet only get as much as a starting sidereal. Astrology is intended as a system in which you want to spend experience and yet you get the most out of it by spending as little experience as you can and then gaming the system. I don't want it to be MtA Magic I want it to be useful. I want to play an expert astrologer and get out what I put in. And right now all it's good for is getting TN 4 for yourself and your circle and then going to town on everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:39:58-07:00","id":108865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108686#post108686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mercury's point is, it'd be more reasonable to expect cheaper, easier to use astrology, than to expect it evolved into something that'd make it worthwhile to invest a thousand experience points in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is &quot; generally not be shit,&quot; &quot;actually useful in an actual games played by actual people&quot; and &quot;not saddled to a horrible, pointless punishment mechanic&quot; assumed to be included in that? Because that's the bulk of my wish list for 3e astrology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Have you ever read a Coik post before, man? lol<br /> -Holden<br /> <br />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/338-coik","name":"Coik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar338_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"611"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T19:51:07-07:00","id":108871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108865#post108865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is &quot; generally not be shit,&quot; &quot;actually useful in an actual games played by actual people&quot; and &quot;not saddled to a horrible, pointless punishment mechanic&quot; assumed to be included in that? Because that's the bulk of my wish list for 3e astrology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it goes without saying that I hope Astrology in 3e is rather more useful. The Colleges are among the best things I've ever seen written for an RPG line, and it's absolutely criminal that they lie fallow so often. I have great hopes for 3e because:<br /> <br /> 1) At the very least, Holden is experienced with Sidereals and knows exactly what was good and less-good in 1e.<br /> 2) The Charms and Astrology chapters will presumably <i>not</i> be written by two different people who have no idea what the other one is doing.<br /> <br /> Seriously, that last thing would be fantastic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T20:12:44-07:00","id":108881,"title":"","content":"Looking at the Exalted at their most basic themes:<br /> <br /> Solars are Chosen of the Sun, and metaphorically shine brightly by literally excelling at all they do.<br /> <br /> Lunars are Chosen of the Moon, and change their shapes as it does.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are Chosen of the Stars, which are known for...kung fu? No, they are associated with foretelling Fate and Fortune, both good and bad. <br /> <br /> So, why shouldn't Seers be the &quot;astrology exalted&quot;? Hell, even the very name ties into the meaning of &quot;ASTROlogy&quot;! While I would like Sids to be stronger sorcerers, I know that's not happening, because of reasons I outlined above. But I would like to see Astrology at least become their thing, even if at the expense of SMA. <br /> <br /> Or does it have to? What if the two systems could be combined? What if Sidereal Martial Arts in 3E became some form of Astrological Martial Arts? What might that look like?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T20:21:28-07:00","id":108888,"title":"","content":"I just hope the stupidity that is &quot;Spider feel overworked, Spider kill Sid's grandma&quot; can die in fire! I don't care that Sidereal are Heaven's bureaucrat so they should be listen to their boss and get their face stomp on, Asna and her bitch children ain't gonna screw with my character and get away with it, reading about her desire to backstab every Sidereal the moment her robot sugar daddy return in Compass: Yu-Shan just fill me with........rage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 04-09-2014, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T20:30:02-07:00","id":108899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108881#post108881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or does it have to? What if the two systems could be combined? What if Sidereal Martial Arts in 3E became some form of Astrological Martial Arts? What might that look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would perfer it be it's own system. Because to some extent it is about understanding how fate works. But you can't make them work in a way that makes astrology useful in a non-combat setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T21:02:27-07:00","id":108928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108881#post108881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or does it have to? What if the two systems could be combined? What if Sidereal Martial Arts in 3E became some form of Astrological Martial Arts? What might that look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a great idea, but here's how I'd do it:<br /> <br /> - Remove College dots, and/or otherwise keep them while linking the cost to the respective Ability<br /> - Tie the Scripture of each Ability to the respective College and fluff the whole thing as the '25 fundamental truths' or something similar<br /> - Merge SMA and Greater Astrology, so that you've got suites of combat charms and also Sorcery-like simple large-scale charm effects<br /> - Re-work Paradox, but keep it as something really horrible to experience. Use that to counter-balance the strongest effects.<br /> - Tie SMA/Astrology styles into the Colleges, and make having the relevant Ability/College the pre-req for each<br /> - You could even separate each College into a 'Martial Style' and an 'Esoteric Style'<br /> <br /> So at that point, when you bought, say, Integrity, you'd also gain points in The Rising Smoke. You'd be able to make an RD from that after a point or two of Integrity, but you'd also be able to purchase Rising Smoke Martial and Esoteric charms. Charcoal March of the Spiders works pretty well for the martial charms, and then Esoteric charms would cover both effects like a charm which granted you bonuses for changing your motivation and An End to Darkness. The second effect would give you Paradox for using it, so you'd do so sparingly.<br /> <br /> (Obviously there's no way in hell anyone's writing 25 SMA styles just to fit there, but SMA is hard to write no matter where you stick the pre-reqs, so eh.)<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> Here's the <i>thing</i> about taking Sidereals and making them 'the Astrology Exalted'- what does that mean? What is it you want Astrology to <i>do</i>?<br /> <br /> Remember that the primary Sidereal competencies and powers come from the charm set. You get yer prophecy from Lore, you get powers to bind gods from Bureaucracy and War, you get dodges and teleporting and the starting tools for pretty much any kit a Sidereal is likely to need in one of those trees. After you're done there, Sorcery serves as the grab-bag of overtly magical powers which aren't really within your themes and Martial Arts serves as the combat-intensive grab-bag of powers which really aren't in <i>anyone's</i> theme. So that stuff is covered- Astrology doesn't need to touch it.<br /> <br /> Astrology, as-is, is just a weird potpurri of things that let you stick TN reductions places, costumes with weirdly unbalanced powers attached and a secondary system of things which are pretty much Astrological-themed sorceries. It's not a coherent power at all, so if you propose to expand it, you've got to figure out which way you think it should be expanded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T21:16:35-07:00","id":108944,"title":"","content":"Hmm. How about this, then:<br /> <br /> Sidereals are not so much the &quot;astrology&quot; Exalted as they are the &quot;enlightenment&quot; Exalted. As many have pointed out in this very thread, it is their Understanding of Esoterica that defines their approach to their powers and capabilities.<br /> <br /> So what if Astrology, through the Colleges, becomes the gateway to that Enlightenment? What if that Enlightenment isn't restricted to any one ability or power, but can be applied to whatever the particular character specializes in?<br /> <br /> This way, we can have the Chosen of Endings who applies her Enlightenment to her Martial Arts, thereby gaining SMA. But we can also have a Chosen of Journeys who applies his Enlightenment to his role as a Teacher, making him a supernal instructor to mortals and Exalts; or a Chosen of Serentiy whose Enlightenment helps her to become a legendary Vizier, guiding the leaders of nations and armies; or a Chosen of Secrets whose Enlightenment aids her in Sorcery, enabling her to reach the Adamant Circle. <br /> <br /> This would be a good way to avoid the &quot;one, true build&quot; problem Sids face, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> (and thanks, Mercury, for actually taking the time to think out how &quot;Sidereal Circle Sorcery&quot; and &quot;Astrological MA&quot; might actually work!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T21:21:18-07:00","id":108949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercury</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=108928#post108928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Here's the <i>thing</i> about taking Sidereals and making them 'the Astrology Exalted'- what does that mean? What is it you want Astrology to <i>do</i>?<br /> <br /> Remember that the primary Sidereal competencies and powers come from the charm set. You get yer prophecy from Lore, you get powers to bind gods from Bureaucracy and War, you get dodges and teleporting and the starting tools for pretty much any kit a Sidereal is likely to need in one of those trees. After you're done there, Sorcery serves as the grab-bag of overtly magical powers which aren't really within your themes and Martial Arts serves as the combat-intensive grab-bag of powers which really aren't in <i>anyone's</i> theme. So that stuff is covered- Astrology doesn't need to touch it.<br /> <br /> Astrology, as-is, is just a weird potpurri of things that let you stick TN reductions places, costumes with weirdly unbalanced powers attached and a secondary system of things which are pretty much Astrological-themed sorceries. It's not a coherent power at all, so if you propose to expand it, you've got to figure out which way you think it should be expanded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Astrology and fate are the same thing. It's a system of bureaucracy for powers and abilities. Like the ability to affect nations. If we are going to make it a system it needs to work like that. I would prefer if Greater astrology wasn't a thing. Expanding the respelendencies would have been a better place to go. Expanding their effects to work with the ability to change nations or affect them easier once you have created a destiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T21:51:07-07:00","id":108958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=107465#post107465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot of people appreciate Sidereals the way they are. IMO, I'm not entirely comfortable with Sidereals being based on the &quot;kung fu hermit&quot; or the &quot;legendary kung fu master&quot;. I think that those archetypes may end up forcing them as NPC's. Sure they also have all the &quot;secret agent&quot; stuff, but in the light of the Ex3 I feel like I can't see Sids as cool as I see solars and lunars now (based on the mythical hero and the mythical beast respectively). If the solar is Hercules, and the lunar could be the nemean lion, who would be the sidereal within this same myth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, champions of the god of war, the god of death, the god of journeys, etc., presumably? Mercury, Venus, Jupiter, Saturn and Mars are all gods in the very same mythology as Hercules and the Hydra, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T01:49:56-07:00","id":109100,"title":"","content":"I like to think that the whole bureaucracy thing for Sidereals is only because that one Goddess of Paperwork (can't remember the name) got high up in the hierarchy of Heaven and reformed it into the Bureaucracy of Heaven. Admittedly now things are for more concise and organized, but it's just such a hassle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T08:47:01-07:00","id":109324,"title":"","content":"It also keeps gods employed. There are a lot of gods who wouldn't have any official position since the Fair Folk took their jerbs, if it weren't for the gigantic and inefficient bureaucracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T09:54:55-07:00","id":109380,"title":"","content":"I think counting up Paradox instead of spending motes has potential and I like that reaching 10 is very bad.<br /> However, Pattern Bites manage to be both boring and stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T14:48:07-07:00","id":109636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=109380#post109380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think counting up Paradox instead of spending motes has potential and I like that reaching 10 is very bad.<br /> However, Pattern Bites manage to be both boring and stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Boring&quot; being the part that really irks me. A mechanic named after anything from Mage: the Ascension has no excuse for being so dull and uninspired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T08:55:02-07:00","id":113356,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea - hitting Paradox can make the Sidereal go out of Fate for an amount of time. Is this actually a flaw for them at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1372,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","user":"Locke","date":". 04-15-2014, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","name":"Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:08:27-07:00","id":113361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=113356#post113356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea - hitting Paradox can make the Sidereal go out of Fate for an amount of time. Is this actually a flaw for them at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. It gives them respite from the annoyances of Arcane Fate and makes them invisible to the scrutiny of their colleagues at the small price of not being able to work Astrology.<br /> <br /> It's also still quite boring, in that it's 100% predictable once it happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:58:11-07:00","id":113389,"title":"","content":"How about just get rid of Paradox completely, they already have the Great Curse ready to whack them, isn't it ? (I'm assuming that the Great Curse mechanic in Manuel: Sidereal is a punishing tool for the ST to slap the PC if they get too annoying)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:19:59-07:00","id":113439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=113389#post113389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about just get rid of Paradox completely, they already have the Great Curse ready to whack them, isn't it ? (I'm assuming that the Great Curse mechanic in Manuel: Sidereal is a punishing tool for the ST to slap the PC if they get too annoying)</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, censure and the infamous Severity 8 offence (lol at original Glories: Maidens typography errors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:38:23-07:00","id":113450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/105491-~sidereal-as-the-martial-art-exalted~?p=113389#post113389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about just get rid of Paradox completely, they already have the Great Curse ready to whack them, isn't it ? (I'm assuming that the Great Curse mechanic in Manuel: Sidereal is a punishing tool for the ST to slap the PC if they get too annoying)</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox has the potential to be an immensely fun mechanic if it takes a hint from it's direct source of inspiration. Think the most bizarre random mishaps/critical fumbles table ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T13:59:04-07:00","id":114320,"title":"","content":"Paradox can also makes a good alternative resources cost to motes or willpower and can't be abused like things which cost Limit can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","nam